The subscription to `dialogRef.closed` in `onCreateList()` was never unsubscribed, causing potential memory leaks when the component is destroyed or when multiple dialogs are opened.

### Changes

- Added `dialogSubscription` property to track the dialog's closed observable subscription
- Modified `onCreateList()` to unsubscribe from previous subscription before assigning new one (handles rapid multiple opens)
- Added cleanup in `ngOnDestroy()` to unsubscribe when component is destroyed

```typescript
onCreateList() {
    const dialogRef = this.dialog.open(ModalNewList, {
        width: '400px',
    });

    // Unsubscribe from previous dialog subscription if it exists
    this.dialogSubscription?.unsubscribe();

    this.dialogSubscription = dialogRef.closed.subscribe(result => {
        if (result && typeof result === 'string') {
            console.log('New list title:', result);
            this.todoService.createList(result);
        }
    });
}

ngOnDestroy() {
    this.listSubscription?.unsubscribe();
    this.dialogSubscription?.unsubscribe();
}
```

